<title>NEW ZEALAND: FCL considers U.K. Paper sale - paper.</title>
<headline>FCL considers U.K. Paper sale - paper.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fletcher Challenge Paper is considering selling its British fine paper producer, U.K. Paper, to focus on more attractive opportunities in north Asia, the New Zealand Herald reported on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Many Asian markets were growing more rapidly off a lower base than markets in North America and Europe, FCL spokesman Barry Akers said.</p>
<p>FCL has in the past acknowledged that its NZ$800 million takeover of U.K. Paper was poorly considered as the British economy and paper prices headed into sharp declines.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
